 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The immersion model is of finite presentation over $S$. Since $S$ is\nquasi-separated, its source is quasi-separated; the selected open\n$Y^\\circ$ is quasi-compact and remains of finite presentation over $S$.\nThe closed-subscheme system then has closed transitions and limit $X$.\nComposition of each finite-presentation closed immersion\n$X_\\alpha\\hookrightarrow Y^\\circ$ with $Y^\\circ\\to S$ is of finite\npresentation. The canonical maps from the limit are closed immersions\nbecause the transition maps are closed immersions.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
